# {ProjectName} — Web-Novel Writing Toolkit (Generic Agent / Web AI)

This project consumes the oh-story skills in the generic file mode. If the current platform has no hooks or custom agents for Claude Code / OpenCode / Codex / ZCode / OpenClaw, the agent can still read `skills/*/SKILL.md` and `skills/*/references/` and execute them directly; runtime hard interception and automatic multi-agent collaboration just will not take effect automatically.

## Skill Routing Table

Prefer naming the skill in natural language; if the platform supports custom commands, the table below can also be mapped to commands.

| Intent | Skill | Description |
|------|-------|------|
| Write long-form / start a book / continue | story-long-write | Long-form web-novel writing (chapter by chapter) |
| Write short-form | story-short-write | Short-form web-novel writing (emotion-driven) |
| Long-form teardown | story-long-analyze | Deep teardown of a long-form novel |
| Short-form teardown | story-short-analyze | Teardown analysis of a short-form novel |
| Long-form market scan | story-long-scan | Long-form novel rankings and market trends |
| Short-form market scan | story-short-scan | Short-form novel rankings and emotional windows |
| De-AI-flavor | story-deslop | Removes AI writing traces |
| Cover | story-cover | Generates cover images |
| Review | story-review | Multi-perspective review; falls back to single-threaded review when custom agents are unavailable |
| Import | story-import | Reverse-imports an existing novel into the project structure |
| Web-novel toolkit | story | Auto-routes ambiguous intent |
| Prepare to write a book / deploy | story-setup | Generic project structure and skill usage entry point |
| Browser login state / scraping | browser-cdp | Browser CDP tool; requires the platform to allow local scripts/browser control |

## File Structure

- `skills/` — project-local skills; the agent should first read the corresponding `SKILL.md`, then read `references/` as needed
- `teardown-lib/` — teardown analysis output directory
- `{BookTitle}/prose/` — long-form novel prose chapters
- `{BookTitle}/prose.md` — short-form novel prose
- `{BookTitle}/setting/` — character settings, world settings
- `{BookTitle}/outline/` — volume outlines, chapter outlines
- `{BookTitle}/tracking/` — context.md, foreshadowing.md, timeline.md, character-state.md
- `{BookTitle}/benchmark/` — benchmark-book analysis

## Generic Usage Conventions

- Have an outline before writing prose: long-form needs `outline/outline_chapter_N*.md`, short-form needs `section-outline.md`.
- Platforms without hooks do not automatically block unauthorized prose writes; the agent must check the outline, context, and tracking files itself when running a writing skill.
- Platforms without custom agents run in solo/direct mode; when a skill calls for agents such as story-architect or narrative-writer, the current agent completes the work directly and notes the fallback in its results.
- **Deslop self-lock** (on hookless platforms this is the only line of defense): after each chapter's prose is written, within the same turn immediately self-check and clear it using the writing skill's "most toxic sentence patterns quick reference + banned words scan" (run `check-ai-patterns.js --check --fail-on=blocking` when node is available); before writing the next chapter, re-check that the previous chapter has no outstanding debt. The only exemption is the user explicitly saying "don't deslop this chapter"; exempt chapters add `<!-- deslop:skip -->` under the title line.
- After a compact / new session, first read `{BookTitle}/tracking/context.md` to restore current writing progress.

## Restoring Context After Compact

Key writing context:
1. Current writing project name and progress
2. Recently discussed character-setting changes
3. List of unresolved foreshadowing
4. The current chapter's emotion/rhythm targets

If `{BookTitle}/tracking/context.md` exists, read it first after a compact to restore context.
